@startuml
title Customer support and incident handling flow (TM Forum Open APIs / ODA)

actor User

box "Engagement Management"
participant "IVR\n(Not an ODA component)" as IVR
actor "Helpdesk Agent" as Agent
participant "Customer Care Portal\n(Not an ODA component)" as Portal
end box

box "Core Systems"
participant "Party Interaction\n(TMFC023)" as PartyInteraction
participant "Permission Management\n(TMFC035)" as PartyRolePermission
participant "Party Problem Management\n(TMFC047)" as PartyProblemMgmt
end box

== Step 1: Customer initiates interaction ==
User -> IVR : 1. Call IVR
IVR -> PartyInteraction : 2. POST /partyInteraction (channel=IVR)
PartyInteraction --> IVR : 3. 201 Created (interaction.id)
IVR -> PartyInteraction : 4. POST /process (Incident Reporting)
PartyInteraction --> IVR : 5. 201 Created (process.id,\nstate=started)
IVR -> User : 6. Present IVR menu options
User -> IVR : 7. Select "Report Problem"

== Step 2: Capture problem details in IVR ==
IVR -> IVR : 8. Capture issue category & basic details
IVR -> PartyInteraction : 9. PATCH /partyInteraction (add IVR inputs)
PartyInteraction --> IVR : 10. 200 OK
IVR -> PartyInteraction : 11. PATCH /process\n(state=IVR_Completed,\ncategory=problem)
PartyInteraction --> IVR : 12. 200 OK

== Step 3: Transfer to Helpdesk Agent ==
IVR -> Agent : 13. Transfer call with captured context
Agent -> Portal : 14. Open customer session
Portal -> PartyInteraction : 15. PATCH /process\n(state=Agent_Handling)
PartyInteraction --> Portal : 16. 200 OK

== Step 4: Customer identification & validation ==
group Validate Customer Identity
Portal -> User : 17. Request customer details
User -> Portal : 18. Provide details
Portal -> PartyRolePermission : 19. GET /partyRole
PartyRolePermission --> Portal : 20. 200 OK (customer profile)
note right of PartyRolePermission
  Permission may
  retrieve Party details from
  Party Management if required.
end note
Portal -> Agent : 21. Display customer details
Agent -> Agent : 22. Validate customer identity
end

== Step 5: Capture detailed problem ==
Agent -> Portal : 23. Enter detailed issue description
Portal -> PartyInteraction : 24. PATCH /partyInteraction (add agent notes)
PartyInteraction --> Portal : 25. 200 OK

== Step 6: Create Party Problem ==
Portal -> PartyProblemMgmt : 26. POST /partyProblem
note right of PartyProblemMgmt
  severity: Critical
  relatedParty: Customer
  channel: IVR + Agent
  description:
  Issue details from
  IVR + Agent
end note
PartyProblemMgmt --> Portal : 27. 201 Created (problem.id)
Portal -> PartyInteraction : 28. PATCH /process\n(state=Problem_Created)
PartyInteraction --> Portal : 29. 200 OK
Portal -> PartyInteraction : 30. PATCH /partyInteraction\n(link problem.id)
PartyInteraction --> Portal : 31. 200 OK

== Step 7: Inform customer ==
Portal -> Agent : 32. Display problem details
Agent -> User : 33. Share problem ID and next steps
@enduml
